### They hear their child ask to go but meet resistance when they try to help them sit.

2 of 38 posts.

One speaker is watching an almost-two-year-old; the other describes their 21-month-old. Requests or poop announcements are followed by running away, screaming, stopping or refusing the potty. The caregiver in the first account suspects toys and television compete for attention; neither account establishes that saying they need to go means willingness to sit.

