### They feel unsettled by the changing routine and by their child growing up.

1 of 38 posts.

This parent's child is in the 18–24-month stage; no exact age is supplied. After the first training day, washed underwear and scheduled potty sits bring an odd feeling about losing the earlier diaper routine. The post links this feeling to the speed of growing up rather than asking for a technique.

