### They want to teach toileting while their child's speech is still limited.

1 of 50 posts.

The parent of a newly two-year-old with about 12 words also has a five-week-old newborn. They describe good understanding, practical nonverbal requests and newly wanting a soiled diaper removed, but no warning before pee. They ask how to teach potty use at this communication stage while caring for both children.

- "My question: any advice you can give me to help me teach my son to learn potty training while not completely verbal just yet and while I’m also taking care of a 5 week old newborn. ALL advice and things that made this process easier for you as a parent is so appreciated! Thanks so much in advance!" [sr043-0039]
- "My son turned 2 on 5/9/2026. He knows about 12 words." [sr043-0040]
- "Immediately after he pees he’ll begin pulling on the crotch of his diaper." [sr043-0042]

**But:** Limited speech is not described as limited understanding: "Despite not speaking much, he’s very smart. If you say “horse, pig, etc” he’ll go to his toys and pick out the animal and bring it to you." [sr043-0041].

